      "side": 1,
      "message": "I need `hmac_sha256()` to calculate signatures (outside of these CLs) anyway and I wanted to avoid copying data back and forth, that\u0027s why it takes span of spans. I also realized that I can reuse it in encryption key deriviation to save some flash space.\n\nIn this case I would need to copy TPM Seed and use subspans to get rollback secret and OTP key. Is that still better that array of spans?",
